				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-34c3d98f elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="34c3d98f" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h2 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Marketing built for <span class="hl">the longest cycle in beauty</span></h2>				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-13ec9434 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="13ec9434" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-585a1d25 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="585a1d25" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4d5f5590 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="4d5f5590" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>Microblading and semi-permanent brow techniques genuinely last 12 to 18 months — the longest result duration of any category we work with, by a wide margin. That single fact flips the usual beauty-marketing playbook on its head: this isn&#8217;t a retention business, it&#8217;s a constant new-client acquisition business, and treating it like a typical repeat-visit salon wastes budget on loyalty tactics that barely apply here.</p>								</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4a447cec elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="4a447cec" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">This is micropigmentation, not a topical treatment</h3>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-16ea5cee elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="16ea5cee" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>Pigment is implanted into the dermis with fine needles — technically a form of tattooing, not a lotion or gel applied to skin. Certification, sterile single-use tools and medical-grade pigments are genuine trust signals here, not marketing fluff, and worth featuring prominently rather than assumed.</p>								</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-6ca118dc elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="6ca118dc" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">The one repeat visit that must never be lost</h3>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-35bea005 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="35bea005" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>The 4-6 week touch-up session is the single predictable rebooking point in an otherwise year-long gap — automated reminders here matter enormously, since a missed touch-up often means a client simply never returns at all.</p>								</div>
				</div>
